course: dictionary
lesson: 4630
title: Words for high places
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hilltop is the top of a hill, the highest part, where you can see far. It is a noun, so it names a thing: a hilltop, or hilltops when there are more than one. When you meet the word, ask yourself: the top of what?
explain: Hilltop can also come before another noun to describe it, as in «a hilltop village» or «a hilltop castle». Here it tells you where the village or castle is: high up, on the top of a hill. In «beacon fires on hilltops», the word hilltops tells you the fires were lit on the tops of hills.
explain: Context gives you clues. In «When fog comes in on hills or moors (wide, open, wild hilltops)», the words wide, open and wild show you that hilltops can be big, empty places. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "the top of a hill" still makes sense, so you have got it.
fact: A hilltop is the top of a hill.
fact: «Hilltops» is the plural, which means more than one hilltop.
fact: Hilltop can come before another noun, as in «a hilltop castle» or «a hilltop village».
fact: «Beacon fires on hilltops» means fires lit on the tops of hills to send a signal.
fact: When you meet an unknown word, read the words around it and swap in your meaning to check.
exercise: «The hilltop castle could be seen for miles.» What is a hilltop? | A kind of castle wall | A deep valley at the bottom of a hill | A river that runs past a hill | *The top of a hill
exercise: Find and copy the plural form of hilltop in «beacon fires on hilltops». | hilltop | fires | beacon | *hilltops
exercise: «When fog comes in on hills or moors, stop, stay together and follow the path.» What should you do? | Hide under a tree | Run as fast as you can to the edge | *Stop, stay together and follow the path | Walk off the path to explore
test: «They lit beacon fires on the hilltop to send a message.» Where were the fires lit? | Inside a cave | *On the hilltop | Under the sea | In a deep valley
test: Which phrase means a village built on the top of a hill? | a village school | a village pond | *a hilltop village | a valley village
exam: «Sam climbed the hilltop path and waited for the view.» What is a hilltop? | A kind of wind | The bottom of a valley | A type of path | *The top of a hill
